From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: the default printer icons (168, 169)

shell32 had no icons 168 and 169 (the default printer, the default
network printer). Epson's printer driver setup (EPSON Printer Utility
Setup, from Epson's official XP-231/XP-230 driver bundle) loads them for
its printer list and divided by zero when two were missing; its setup now
runs. They are the printer icon.

Test: test/printdrv-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_SHELLICONS).
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shell32.rc
@@ -653,6 +653,15 @@
 /* @makedep: resources/printer.ico */
 IDI_SHELL_REMOTE_PRINTER ICON resources/printer.ico
 
+/* the default printer's icons: makers' setup programs load them (Epson's) */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SHELLICONS
+/* @makedep: resources/printer.ico */
+IDI_SHELL_DEFAULT_PRINTER ICON resources/printer.ico
+
+/* @makedep: resources/printer.ico */
+IDI_SHELL_DEFAULT_REMOTE_PRINTER ICON resources/printer.ico
+#endif
+
 /* FIXME: Following resource is not yet added */
 /* @makedep: resources/printer.ico */
 IDI_SHELL_TO_FILE_PRINTER ICON resources/printer.ico
